{"name":"Pink Chintz","hex":"#efbecf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"chintz","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A painted or stained calico fabric, originally produced in India, and known for its brightly colored designs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chintz"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chintz","blocks":[{"text":"Chintz is a woodblock printed, painted, stained or glazed calico textile that originated in Golconda in the 15th century. The cloth is printed with designs featuring flowers and other patterns in different colours, typically on a light, plain background."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Jacket_and_shawl_in_chintz%2C_skirt_in_glazed_printed_cotton%2C_1770-1800._MoMu_-_Fashion_Museum_Province_of_Antwerp%2C_www.momu.be._Photo_by_Hugo_Maertens%2C_Bruges..jpg/330px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chintz","wikidata":"Q1074462"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0